+/*
+ * VNBox: movies played by the browser page
+ *
+ * When a graph renders a file the page can decode (an MPEG-1 program stream), RenderFile adds
+ * this filter alone instead of a source, splitter, decoders and renderers. It owns a real video
+ * window (window.c: owner, position, message drain and full screen work as with the video
+ * renderer) and hands the file, the window's screen rectangle, state changes, seeks and volume to
+ * VNBox through /dev/vnbox-movie; the page draws the movie over the canvas at that rectangle and
+ * says when it has ended, which becomes EC_COMPLETE. Anything else, or no page, takes Wine's
+ * normal path.
+ *
